{
  "_comment": "The twelve hand-sign categories. 'diagram' drives the schematic shown in the app: each hand lists the state of thumb, index, middle, ring, pinky as 'up' (extended), 'fold' (curled) or 'lock' (interlocked with the other hand). 'recognition' configures the built-in recogniser that works without training: finger states come from the diagram (hand 'left' = role a, 'right' = role b; the two detected hands are matched to the roles whichever way fits best), and 'rules' are soft conditions on named pose features (see app/computer_vision/pose.py) - 'min'/'max' with a 'soft' margin and a 'weight'. An optional 'threshold' overrides the default confidence needed (0.62, adjusted by the recognition mode). The poses are game-defined guides based on commonly shown references; edit them freely.",
